#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""watch-forks-menubar — macOS menu bar widget for live fork counts.

Polls the same ps surfaces as ~/bin/watch-forks (via importlib reuse), shows
the top fork count + total CPU in the menu bar, and renders the top-N
offenders in the dropdown. Each offender opens a submenu with PID/CPU/STAT
details plus SIGTERM and SIGKILL actions (with confirm dialog).

Persisted settings: interval, top N, and pause state are stored in
  ~/Library/Application Support/watch-forks-menubar/settings.json
and reloaded at launch.

Live-updates while the dropdown is open: the timer is scheduled in
NSRunLoopCommonModes (so it fires during NSEventTrackingRunLoopMode menu
tracking), and a fixed pool of NSMenuItem rows is mutated in place each
tick — never cleared — so the open menu stays open and just refreshes.

Launch:  ~/bin/watch-forks-menubar &
Quit:    menu → Quit (or pkill -f watch-forks-menubar)
"""
